  "post": {
    "caption": "Turquoise's name means Turkish stone, because it probably reached Europe through Turkey. Its classic sky blue is called Persian blue, Egyptians mined it in Sinai thousands of years ago, and bracelets with turquoise from King Djer's tomb are about 5,000 years old. It is soft, only 5 to 6 on the Mohs scale, and skin oils and cosmetics can discolor it. Turquoise is the December birthstone.",
